{
 "method": "ftsspec_830626_2 (air mass 5.37) and _3 (3.09) are two scans of the same Sun on one day. If the telluric correction is right their corrected spectra agree; where they do not at telluric pixels, that is correction error, measured without anyone else's product. #3 is put on #2's pixels after one velocity shift per run that aligns their solar lines (the README warns of a wavenumber-scale shift, and the Sun's line-of-sight velocity changes between scans). The ratio is normalized by a running mean over pixels where neither file has telluric absorption, then scored as score_telluric_correction.py scores flatness: rms of (ratio - 1) at pixels clear of solar lines where the first file's relative transmission is below 0.97 and both are at least 0.15, interior only. An error identical in both corrected spectra cancels, so this bounds the correction error from below; since the error grows with air mass, most of it shows.",
